    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"I started thinking: Was Gabrielle Chanel's life itself a fairy tale? I discovered a small book in her library—'Les Fées, Contes des Contes'—and thought, could we collaborate with the haute couture atelier to give fashion the power to tell stories?\" — Matthieu Blazy",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "(Swipe left or right to browse more images)",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The classic Chanel suit opened the show, with clean lines and structured tailoring, crafted from raised-lace embroidered with magic bean motifs and accented with sheer silk tulle. Models carried a copy of 'Les Fées, Contes des Contes' from Gabrielle Chanel's library, and the book's whimsy translated into intricate details: vines climbing up heels, a compact evening bag shaped like a sleeping bear, and buttons depicting the ugly duckling's transformation into a swan.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
